# A follower uses up a portal's last charge. At the entrance to Mud School (3700), a gate (25) with two charges
# leads to the temple (3001). Outlaw (18) follows Decimus (10); Pupil (10) stays behind. Decimus enters: his charge
# leaves one, and Outlaw, led through after him, uses it up, so Outlaw's own do_enter extracts the gate. Then
# Decimus's do_enter, which led him, read the freed gate again: in its follower loop, in "fades out of existence",
# and in a second extract_obj (#26): Pupil saw the gate fade twice, and the log said "Extract_obj: obj 25 not
# found". Now a follower leaves a gate its leader is leading them through for the leader's do_enter to fade and
# extract: Decimus and Pupil each see it fade once.
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
goto 3700
@connect out
Outlaw
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect pup
Pupil
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
transfer decimus 3700
transfer outlaw 3700
transfer pupil 3700
@as out
follow decimus
@obj 25 3700 2 0 0 3001 -1
@as dec
enter gate
look
@as pup
look
